# tally 2.1.8 (R9, the gate's rest 3), L §5.18, §2.4: a partial line's money coefficient prints with its minor
# unit's digits (10.00 PLN ×), as money times a whole number does; scaled by a num it is a num PLN (20 PLN ×), as a
# known product prints.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place market: outside lives 2026-01-01..
index ks = [a, b]
input amt: money PLN
input bday: date
input pday: date
input fx: num PLN/EUR
input rate: num
input r2: num
input h: money PLN
input k: money PLN
input c[x in ks]: bool

move pay: transfers
  on pday
  leg cash from market to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = ?"how much" "s"
  bday = 2026-01-10 "s"
  pday = 2026-02-05 "s"
  fx = 4 PLN/EUR "s"
  rate = 2 "s"
  r2 = ?"what rate" "s"
  h = ?"what is h" "s"
  k = 10.00 PLN "s"
  c[a] = true "s"
  c[b] = ?"is b" "s"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask mc1: k * r2 partial
ask mc2: r2 * k + k partial
ask mc3: k * r2 * rate partial
=== expect
mc1: 10.00 PLN × ?"what rate" (r2)
  cut 2026-06-10
mc2: 10.00 PLN + 10.00 PLN × ?"what rate" (r2)
  cut 2026-06-10
mc3: 20 PLN × ?"what rate" (r2)
  cut 2026-06-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD input bday is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input c is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input fx is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input h is read by nothing
